From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapi: ISpStream and ISpeechFileStream, audio format objects, resource manager

sapi: ISpStream and ISpeechFileStream, audio format objects, resource manager

All of these were FIXME stubs returning E_NOTIMPL (or E_NOINTERFACE with a
FIXME).

- ISpStream (SpStream, and the ISpStream view of SpFileStream): a wrapper
  around an IStream plus a format. Before SetBaseStream/BindToFile every
  member reports SPERR_UNINITIALIZED; SetBaseStream checks its arguments
  (E_INVALIDARG, SPERR_UNSUPPORTED_FORMAT for a format that is neither
  SPDFID_Text nor SPDFID_WaveFormatEx) and a second call is
  SPERR_ALREADY_INITIALIZED; GetFormat returns the GUID and a CoTaskMem copy
  of the WAVEFORMATEX; Read/Write/Seek/SetSize/CopyTo/Commit/Revert/
  LockRegion/UnlockRegion/Stat go to the base stream; Clone clones the base
  stream into a new ISpStream with the same format; Close releases the base
  stream and makes the object uninitialized again.
- BindToFile opens or creates a file for the four SPFILEMODEs. A RIFF/WAVE
  file is presented as its data only (offset 0 is the first data byte) and
  names its own format; creating a wave file writes the header and
  patches the RIFF and data sizes on Commit/Close; any other file is raw data
  in SPDFID_Text (or the format given). SPFM_CREATE on an existing file is
  ERROR_FILE_EXISTS, a missing file ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND, creating without
  a format SPERR_FORMAT_NOT_SPECIFIED.
- ISpeechFileStream: IDispatch through the SAPI type library (type info
  count, type info, names, invoke) and Format, Read, Write, Seek, Open and
  Close on top of the ISpStream. Read returns a byte array, Write takes a
  byte array (or a 16/32 bit integer array), Seek takes any number and
  returns an integer. Opening a new file with no Format set uses 22 kHz 16
  bit mono PCM.
- ISpeechAudioFormat and ISpeechWaveFormatEx objects (new audioformat.c):
  Type maps the SpeechAudioFormatType PCM, A-law and mu-law formats to and
  from a wave format, Guid, GetWaveFormatEx/SetWaveFormatEx, and the
  wave format properties with ExtraData.
- ISpResourceManager: one manager per process (CoCreateInstance returns the
  same object), SetObject/QueryService/GetObject keep a table of services
  (SetObject(NULL) removes one, GetObject creates a missing one from the CLSID
  and keeps it, QueryService says SPERR_NOT_FOUND), and it answers
  IServiceProvider.
- The class factory's QueryInterface and LockServer no longer log FIXMEs and
  the unknown-interface messages of the objects above are warnings.

